# Line-ending policy for the INCM Phase 0 repository.
#
# This machine runs git with core.autocrlf=true, which silently rewrites CRLF to
# LF when a file is staged. data/metadata/.generated_manifest.json records the
# SHA-256 digest of every generated artefact, and the inventory script re-checks
# those digests as a reproducibility guarantee. Any byte rewritten by git would
# therefore make a fresh clone fail the project's own integrity check, so the
# generated artefacts below are pinned to "store exactly what is on disk".
#
# Syntax note: .gitattributes takes only <pattern> <attributes> pairs.

# --- Generated data and results: byte-frozen, never eol-converted ------------
# The CSV inventories are emitted LF; the report and JSON summaries are emitted
# CRLF by Python's text-mode writer on Windows. Both are covered by the manifest,
# so both must round-trip through git unchanged.
data/metadata/** -text
results/dataset_inventory/** -text
*.csv -text
*.json -text

# --- Handwritten documentation: keep the authored bytes ----------------------
docs/*.md -text

# --- Python sources: normalise to LF in the repository -----------------------
# No hash covers these, so normalising is safe and keeps diffs stable whether a
# contributor's checkout is Windows or Linux.
*.py text eol=lf

# --- Payloads that eol heuristics would corrupt ------------------------------
*.png -text
*.pdf -text
*.gz -text
*.zip -text
